  "launches": [
    {
      "id": 102597,
      "title": "9 Mothers - AI mission systems",
      "tagline": "EDDA - is a tiny robot that protects soldiers and critical assets from Group 1 suicide drones",
      "body": "We make AI mission systems for the DoW.\n\n![uploaded image](/media/?type=post&id=102597&key=user_uploads/1373/31af3058-9bd9-48b5-8b9a-4840055d12f9)\n\nOur first product - EDDA - is a tiny robot that protects soldiers and critical assets from Group 1 suicide drones. We are building it small enough and cheap enough to put that protection on everything: every vehicle, every position, every asset. EDDA defeats fast group 1 threats that fielded systems consistently miss. Operators evaluating it have told us it's the only system that's stopped fast Group 1 - we'll let them speak for themselves when they can.\n\n<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KBGBUmwgpL0>\n\nWhy this? We were watching people die in the Russia-Ukraine conflict, and ended up researching the state of the union on defeating suicide drones. It was insanely bad - over-focus on RF, EW, and larger systems - all with obvious flaws. Nothing was working, all demos were of slow speed or static drones. RF &amp; EW are somewhere between dead-ends and table-stakes, and the larger systems had many flaws. So, we felt compelled to fix it.\n\n<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PEgJkZTNcks>\n\nThe U.S. and allies are up-against this threat with no viable solution, until now. We have multiple contracts, and have sold and delivered multiple systems.\n\nOur next 3 products follow the same vein - delivering working systems at low SWaPc.",
      "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/launches/Qgn-9-mothers-ai-mission-systems",
      "votes": 10,
      "created_at": "2026-06-05T18:10:21.843Z"
    }
  ]
